@api = http://localhost:5180

### Indexed films and configured models
GET {{api}}/movies/stats

### Plot only
POST {{api}}/movies/search
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "a man relives the same day over and over" }

### Plot + criteria: the filter is what makes a vague description findable
POST {{api}}/movies/search
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "astronauts on a dangerous mission in space", "releasedFrom": 1990, "releasedTo": 1999, "genre": "drama", "top": 5 }

### Brute force vs pgvector index vs index + filter
POST {{api}}/movies/search/compare
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "astronauts on a dangerous mission in space", "releasedFrom": 1990, "releasedTo": 1999, "genre": "drama" }

### Agent, tool mode: the model fills in the criteria itself
POST {{api}}/movies/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "a 90s sci-fi film where astronauts are stranded", "mode": "tool" }

### Agent, context mode: TextSearchProvider searches with the raw question before every call
POST {{api}}/movies/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "a 90s sci-fi film where astronauts are stranded", "mode": "context" }

### 400: domain rule broken
POST {{api}}/movies/search
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "space", "releasedFrom": 2000, "releasedTo": 1990 }
